## Architecture governance

For architecture selection, system decomposition, design documents, cross-domain pattern mapping, architecture review, or any change that creates, splits, merges, moves, or renames three or more sibling source files or changes package/directory topology, invoke `$architecture-design` and follow its gates before implementation.

Repository-specific additions:

- Preserve explicit user constraints and exclusions.
- Ground claims in repository evidence and primary documentation.
- Do not create large scaffolds before architecture Gate G6 passes.
- Include tracked and untracked candidate source files in the source-topology
  map; reject one-type/operation/phase/helper/validation-per-file splitting
  unless independent lifecycle and contract evidence exists.
- Run the architecture-enforce capability preflight and full audit before and
  after repository edits. No baseline, exclusion, disabled/advisory gate,
  threshold override, or exception is acceptance proof.
- Never suppress lint/check failures with ignore directives, disabled rules or
  providers/jobs, lowered severity, `allow-failure`, `continue-on-error`,
  excluded paths, baseline edits, or weakened/deleted tests. Fix the owning
  cause; if a tool is wrong, provide a minimal reproducer and obtain explicit
  policy authorization while keeping the architecture gate blocked.
- Place generated architecture artifacts under `<project architecture path>`.
- Run `python <skill path>/scripts/skill_checks.py report <report>` before acceptance.
